[[3,63,0,"<aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Follow the safety instructions\n(\n                                                         <a href=\"#/2891803\">5040A</a>\n                                                          ).</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside>"],[3,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2891945\">5550B30</a></p><p>Drain the coolant fluid (refer to op. \n\n                                          <a href=\"#/2891804\">5040A10</a>\n                                           ).</p><p>1. Undo the bolts and the nut.</p><p>2. Disconnect the pipe connectors.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Seal the disconnected connectors,\nusing suitable plugs, to prevent humidity and impurities from entering\nthe system.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>3. Release the pipe from the retaining bands.</p><p>4. Remove the pipe.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2035221.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[3,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the pipe is not\ndamaged or cracked.</p><p>Reposition the pipe and fix it using the\nretaining bands.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Replace the O-rings for the connectors.\nOnly use green coloured seals, resistant to R134A coolant fluid.\nLubricate the thread of the connectors using anti-freeze.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Connect the pipe connectors.</p><p>Tighten the bolt and the nut fixing the\ncondenser connector and the intermediate connector.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT SYSTEM FITTINGS</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.9</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Tighten the bolt fixing the pipe connector\nto the compressor.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>Compressor pipe connector</p></td><td><p>M10 x 1.25</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>3.5</p></td></tr></table></div><p><a href=\"#/2891945\">5550B30</a></p><p>Repressurize the coolant fluid (refer to\nop. \n                                          <a href=\"#/2891804\">5040A10</a>\n                                           ).</p>"]]